con Martin\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Italian imperative | Italian grammar B1 | Italiano con Martin\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Learn the Italian imperative with examples and interactive exercises.\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://italianoconmartin.com/en/grammar/b1/the-italian-imperative.html\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://italianoconmartin.com/assets/social-card.svg\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Italian imperative | Italian grammar B1 | Italiano con Martin\"><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Learn the Italian imperative with examples and interactive exercises.\"><meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://italianoconmartin.com/assets/social-card.svg\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../styles.css\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../assets/grammar-lesson.css\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"../../../favicon.png\" type=\"image/png\"><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"../../../apple-touch-icon.png\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"LearningResource\",\"name\":\"Italian imperative\",\"url\":\"https://italianoconmartin.com/en/grammar/b1/the-italian-imperative.html\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}</script></head><body data-lesson=\"martin-imperativo-b1\"><header class=\"site-header\"><div class=\"container nav-wrap\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"/en/\"><img class=\"brand-avatar\" src=\"../../../assets/martin-photo.svg\" alt=\"Martin\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" decoding=\"async\"><span>Italiano con Martin</span></a><details class=\"language-switcher\"><summary aria-label=\"Language\"><span class=\"language-flag\" aria-hidden=\"true\">🇬🇧</span><span class=\"language-current\">English</span><span class=\"language-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⌄</span></summary><div class=\"language-options\"><a href=\"/grammatica/b1/imperativo.html\" hreflang=\"it\" lang=\"it\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇮🇹</span><span>Italiano</span></a><a href=\"/en/grammar/b1/the-italian-imperative.html\" hreflang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" aria-current=\"page\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇬🇧</span><span>English</span></a><a href=\"/es/gramatica/b1/el-imperativo-italiano.html\" hreflang=\"es\" lang=\"es\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇪🇸</span><span>Español</span></a><a href=\"/fr/grammaire/b1/limperatif-italien.html\" hreflang=\"fr\" lang=\"fr\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇫🇷</span><span>Français</span></a><a href=\"/cs/gramatika/b1/italsky-imperativ.html\" hreflang=\"cs\" lang=\"cs\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇨🇿</span><span>Čeština</span></a><a href=\"/pl/gramatyka/b1/tryb-rozkazujacy-po-wlosku.html\" hreflang=\"pl\" lang=\"pl\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇵🇱</span><span>Polski</span></a><a href=\"/tr/dilbilgisi/b1/italyanca-emir-kipi.html\" hreflang=\"tr\" lang=\"tr\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇹🇷</span><span>Türkçe</span></a><a href=\"/de/grammatik/b1/der-italienische-imperativ.html\" hreflang=\"de\" lang=\"de\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇩🇪</span><span>Deutsch</span></a><a href=\"/ja/bunpo/b1/イタリア語の命令法.html\" hreflang=\"ja\" lang=\"ja\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🇯🇵</span><span>日本語</span></a></div></details><nav><a href=\"/en/grammar/\">Grammar</a><a href=\"/en/readings/\">Readings</a><a href=\"/en/vocabulary/\">Vocabulary</a><a class=\"about-link\" href=\"/en/about-us/\">About us</a><a class=\"nav-cta\" href=\"https://preply.com/it/tutor/5086125\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Book on Preply</a></nav></div></header><main><section class=\"page-intro\"><div class=\"container lesson-shell\"><p class=\"breadcrumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> / <a href=\"/en/grammar/\">Grammar</a> / B1 / Italian imperative</p><p class=\"eyebrow\">Grammar B1</p><h1>Italian imperative</h1><p class=\"lead\">Give instructions, advice, invitations and directions in a natural way: listen, take, leave, don't do.</p><div class=\"lesson-nav\"><a href=\"#regola\">Rule</a><a href=\"#tabella\">Table</a><a href=\"#esempi\">Examples</a><a href=\"#esercizi\">Exercises</a></div><div class=\"pdf-downloads\" aria-label=\"PDF downloads\"><a class=\"button secondary\" href=\"/pdf/en/the-italian-imperative-b1.pdf\" download=\"\">PDF B1</a></div></div></section><section class=\"section compact-top\"><div class=\"container lesson-shell\"><article class=\"lesson-box\" id=\"regola\"><h2>When is it used?</h2><p>We use the imperative for instructions, invitations, advice and direct requests. The tone depends a lot on the situation.</p><div class=\"example-grid\"><div class=\"example\"><strong>Istruzione</strong><br>Gira a destra.</div><div class=\"example\"><strong>Invito</strong><br>Entra, per favore.</div><div class=\"example\"><strong>Consiglio</strong><br>Dormi un po'.</div><div class=\"example\"><strong>Divieto</strong><br>Non parlare adesso.</div></div></article><article class=\"lesson-box\" id=\"tabella\"><h2>Shapes with you and you</h2><table class=\"conj-table\"><thead><tr><th>Infinito</th><th>Tu</th><th>Voi</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>parlare</td><td>parla</td><td>parlate</td></tr><tr><td>prendere</td><td>prendi</td><td>prendete</td></tr><tr><td>partire</td><td>parti</td><td>partite</td></tr><tr><td>fare</td><td>fa' / fai</td><td>fate</td></tr><tr><td>andare</td><td>va' / vai</td><td>andate</td></tr><tr><td>dire</td><td>di'</td><td>dite</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"mini-note\"><strong>Negative with you:</strong> not + infinitive. Don't speak, don't take, don't leave.</p></article><article class=\"lesson-box\" id=\"esempi\"><h2>With pronouns</h2><p>With the affirmative imperative, the pronoun is attached to the end.</p><div class=\"example-grid\"><div class=\"example\">Prendi il libro. Prendilo.</div><div class=\"example\">Ascolta me. Ascoltami.</div><div class=\"example\">Mandate la foto. Mandatela.</div><div class=\"example\">Non lo prendere. / Non prenderlo.</div></div></article><article class=\"lesson-box\"><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class=\"mistake-grid\"><div class=\"mistake\"><strong>Non: tu parla italiano</strong>Ma: parla italiano.</div><div class=\"mistake\"><strong>Non: non parla!</strong>Ma: non parlare!</div><div class=\"mistake\"><strong>Non: lo prendi!</strong>Ma: prendilo!</div><div class=\"mistake\"><strong>Non: andi!</strong>Ma: va'! / vai!</div></div></article><article class=\"lesson-box\" id=\"esercizi\"><h2>Exercises with immediate feedback</h2><p>Complete with the correct imperative.</p><div id=\"exercise-list\"><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"parla\" data-hint=\"With you, talking becomes talk.\"><label>1. ___ più lentamente, per favore. (parlare)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"prendi\" data-hint=\"With you, taking becomes taking.\"><label>2. ___ l'autobus numero 4. (prendere)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"partite\" data-hint=\"With you, leaving becomes matches.\"><label>3. ___ domani mattina. (voi, partire)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"non parlare\" data-hint=\"Negative with tu: not + infinitive.\"><label>4. ___ adesso! (tu, parlare, negativo)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"ascoltami\" data-hint=\"Pronoun mi attached to the verb.\"><label>5. ___ un momento. (ascoltare + mi)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"prendilo\" data-hint=\"Take + it becomes take it.\"><label>6. Il libro è sul tavolo: ___. (prendere + lo)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"fate\" data-hint=\"With you, doing becomes doing.\"><label>7. ___ attenzione! (voi, fare)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"va\" data-alt=\"vai|va'\" data-hint=\"Go with you: go or go.\"><label>8. ___ a casa, sei stanco. (tu, andare)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"dite\" data-hint=\"With you, saying becomes saying.\"><label>9. ___ la verità. (voi, dire)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div><div class=\"exercise\" data-answer=\"non aprire\" data-hint=\"Negative with tu: not + infinitive.\"><label>10. ___ la finestra. (tu, aprire, negativo)</label><input autocomplete=\"off\"><div class=\"feedback\"></div></div></div><div class=\"score-card\"><div><strong>Your result</strong><p id=\"score-text\">0 correct answers out of 10</p></div><strong id=\"score-percent\">0%</strong></div><div class=\"exercise-actions\"><button class=\"reset-btn\" id=\"reset-exercises\" type=\"button\">Start again</button><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://preply.com/it/tutor/5086125\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Train with Martin</a></div></article></div></section><section class=\"conversion-section teacher-cta-section\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"teacher-cta-heading\"><div><p class=\"eyebrow\">Italiano con Martin</p><h2>Choose who to learn Italian with</h2></div><p>Two teachers, two perspectives. Choose the approach that best matches your interests.</p></div><div class=\"teacher-cta-options\"><article class=\"teacher-cta\"><img src=\"../../../assets/martin-portrait.webp\" alt=\"Martin\" width=\"800\" height=\"1067\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><div><strong>Martin</strong><span>Science, technology and etymology</span></div><a class=\"button light\" href=\"https://preply.com/it/tutor/5086125\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn with Martin</a></article><article class=\"teacher-cta\"><img src=\"../../../assets/licia-portrait.webp\" alt=\"Licia\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><div><strong>Licia</strong><span>Art, patience and grammar</span></div><a class=\"button light\" href=\"https://preply.in/LICIA6IT2176799611?ts=17865248\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn with Licia</a></article></div><div class=\"teacher-cta-links\"><a href=\"/en/about-us/\">Meet Martin and Licia</a><a href=\"https://wa.me/59167434075?text=Hello%2C%20I%20would%20like%20information%20about%20Italian%20lessons%20with%20Martin%20or%20Licia.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Message us on WhatsApp</a></div></div></section></main><footer><div class=\"container footer-grid\"><div><strong>Italiano con Martin</strong><p>Clear grammar, graded readings and online lessons.</p></div><div><a href=\"/en/grammar/\">Grammar</a><a href=\"/en/readings/\">Readings</a><a href=\"/en/vocabulary/\">Vocabulary</a><a class=\"about-link\" href=\"/en/about-us/\">About us</a></div></div></footer><script src=\"../../../assets/grammar-exercises.js\"></script><script src=\"../../../script.js\"></script>\n</body></html>";
